WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:04.190
Alice looked around the table.

2
00:00:04.191 --> 00:00:06.751
There were many place settings.

3
00:00:06.752 --> 00:00:12.663
But the only ones at the table were the Hatter, the March Hare, and the Dormouse.

4
00:00:12.664 --> 00:00:16.787
"Why are there so many dishes?" Alice asked the Hatter.

5
00:00:16.788 --> 00:00:22.897
"It's always six o'clock, so that means it's always time for tea," he explained.

6
00:00:22.898 --> 00:00:26.411
"We don't have time to wash the dishes."

7
00:00:26.412 --> 00:00:32.872
"So when you need clean dishes, you move to the next place setting?" Alice asked.

8
00:00:32.873 --> 00:00:37.137
The Hatter nodded in agreement. "Exactly."

9
00:00:37.138 --> 00:00:43.844
Alice thought about this for a moment.

10
00:00:43.845 --> 00:00:49.352
"But what happens when you come back to where you started?"

11
00:00:49.353 --> 00:00:53.455
"Let's change the subject," the March Hare said.

12
00:00:53.456 --> 00:00:58.691
"I'm getting bored. I think the young lady should tell us a story."

13
00:00:58.692 --> 00:01:01.440
"What?" Alice shook her head.

14
00:01:01.441 --> 00:01:04.515
"But I don't know any stories."

15
00:01:04.516 --> 00:01:11.855
"Then the Dormouse will tell us one," the March Hare and the Hatter said together. They

16
00:01:11.856 --> 00:01:17.251
pinched the Dormouse on both sides at once. "Tell

17
00:01:17.252 --> 00:01:20.946
us a story," the March Hare said. "Yes,

18
00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:24.718
please do," Alice begged. "And

19
00:01:24.719 --> 00:01:26.546
be quick about it. Or

20
00:01:26.547 --> 00:01:30.616
you'll fall asleep before you're done," the Hatter added. The

21
00:01:30.617 --> 00:01:34.332
Dormouse sat up straight and began to talk. "Once

22
00:01:34.333 --> 00:01:39.160
upon a time, there were three little sisters. Their

23
00:01:39.161 --> 00:01:42.472
names were Elsie, Lacie, and Tillie. They

24
00:01:42.473 --> 00:01:46.323
lived at the bottom of a well, and—" "Did

25
00:01:46.324 --> 00:01:49.161
they get hungry down there?" Alice asked. She

26
00:01:49.162 --> 00:01:55.269
was always interested in what people ate and drank. The

27
00:01:55.270 --> 00:02:00.355
Dormouse thought for a moment or two. "They

28
00:02:00.356 --> 00:02:05.327
lived on molasses," he finally said. Alice

29
00:02:05.328 --> 00:02:07.658
shook her head in disbelief. "Those

30
00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:11.095
girls couldn't have done that," she said gently. "That

31
00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:14.329
would have made them ill." "Yes,

32
00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:20.151
they were very ill," the Dormouse said. Alice

33
00:02:20.152 --> 00:02:24.760
tried to imagine what it would be like to live in a well. But

34
00:02:24.761 --> 00:02:26.408
she couldn't. "Why

35
00:02:26.409 --> 00:02:30.789
did they live at the bottom of a well?" "Have

36
00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:35.067
some more tea," the March Hare said to her. "I've

37
00:02:35.068 --> 00:02:38.100
had nothing so far," Alice said. "So

38
00:02:38.101 --> 00:02:40.675
I can't have more ."

39
00:02:40.676 --> 00:02:43.968
"Nonsense!" the March Hare said.

40
00:02:43.969 --> 00:02:49.084
"If you have nothing, anything is more than that."

41
00:02:49.085 --> 00:02:59.740
Alice didn't know what to say to this.

42
00:02:59.741 --> 00:03:04.101
So she helped herself to tea, and bread and butter.

43
00:03:04.102 --> 00:03:07.948
Then she turned to the Dormouse and repeated her question.

44
00:03:07.949 --> 00:03:11.608
"Why did the sisters live at the bottom of a well?"

45
00:03:11.609 --> 00:03:15.829
Again the Dormouse took a few moments to think.

46
00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:20.834
"Because it was a molasses well."

47
00:03:20.835 --> 00:03:26.679
"There's no such thing!" Alice said angrily.

48
00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.755
The Hatter and March Hare shushed her.

49
00:03:29.756 --> 00:03:31.782
The Dormouse frowned.

50
00:03:31.783 --> 00:03:41.379
"If you can't be nice," he said, "you can finish the story yourself."

51
00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:47.254
"No, please go on. I promise to stay quiet and listen," Alice said. "I

52
00:03:47.255 --> 00:03:53.309
want a clean cup," the Hatter interrupted. So

53
00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:59.800
they all moved one place to the right, and the Dormouse went on with his story. "The

54
00:03:59.801 --> 00:04:07.225
sisters were drawing things beginning with the letter M such as—" "Why

55
00:04:07.226 --> 00:04:11.766
with an M ?" Alice asked. "I don't think—"

56
00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:15.552
"Then you shouldn't talk," the Hatter said.

57
00:04:15.553 --> 00:04:20.212
This bit of rudeness was more than Alice could bear.

58
00:04:20.213 --> 00:04:23.404
She got up in disgust.

59
00:04:23.405 --> 00:04:28.193
As she walked away, the Dormouse fell asleep.

60
00:04:28.194 --> 00:04:33.034
The Hatter and the March Hare didn't seem to notice her leaving.

61
00:04:33.035 --> 00:04:37.716
Alice looked back several times, hoping they would call after her.

62
00:04:37.717 --> 00:04:44.867
But now they were busy trying to put the Dormouse into the teapot.

63
00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:49.492
"I'll never go there again," Alice said as she walked through the woods.

64
00:04:49.493 --> 00:04:55.360
"That was the dumbest tea party ever."

